  "notes": [
    "The index was rebuilt on 2026-11-27 with onnxruntime-web (WebAssembly), the runtime the browser uses, so a question searched in the demo gets the same vector as here (cosine > 0.9999). The earlier vectors came from onnxruntime-node, whose 8-bit kernels round differently (cosine 0.996). Graph only and hybrid kept their recall@5 and MRR; vectors only went from 78% to 73%. The 111 answers whose search notes changed were asked and judged again; the other 259 have the same inputs and were kept.",
    "Before this run, a rehearsal bug answered the 40 test questions once, and those answers were read. Nothing was tuned on them: the search weights were fixed earlier on the 10 tuning questions, and the one change made afterwards (a passage per note that words its typed links and aliases, which live in the frontmatter) came from the tuning questions q-001, q-002, q-008 and q-009, which failed for that reason. The bug is fixed and tested: a rehearsal never answers a test question.",
    "Graph only finds slightly more of the expected notes in its top 5 than hybrid (93% against 91%), but hybrid ranks them higher (MRR 0.87 against 0.78) and answers more of the answerable questions (96% against 94%).",
    "The judge check samples half of its answers among those with a sentence the judge did not fully support, so it looks at the judge where it matters; it is not a random sample of all answers."
